<p></p><center><table width=3D"610" border=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadd=
ing=3D"4">
  <tbody><tr>
    <td width=3D"100%" align=3D"CENTER" bgcolor=3D"#000000"><table width=3D=
"600" border=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"4">
        <tbody><tr>
          <td width=3D"100%" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff">
            <p></p><center><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20050222=
044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dcTitle.jpg" width=3D"576" =
height=3D"146" align=3D"BOTTOM" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3"></center=
><p></p>

            <p></p><center><font size=3D"+3" face=3D"Times New Roman">Part =
I: It's
            a Strange Invitation.</font></center><p></p>

            <p></p><center><i><font face=3D"Arial">(Almost everything in th=
is entire
            series is true. As the story progresses, I will let you, the
            reader, in on the things that didn't actually happen. Some, but
            not all, of the names have been changed.)</font></i></center><p=
></p>

            <p><b><font size=3D"+1" face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.=
archive.org/web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1=
I.gif" width=3D"21" height=3D"46" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizefl=
ag=3D"3"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20050222044718im_/http://h=
ellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dcauthor.jpg" width=3D"201" height=3D"94" ali=
gn=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3"></font><font face=3D"Arial"=
>had
            been working at the Tibetan Freedom Concert in Washington D.C.
            for two weeks. When I returned home, the first thing I did was
            check the E-mail that had accumulated unchecked, breeding like
            rabbits. Amongst the avalanche of debt reduction scams, porn-si=
te
            spam, shady home businesses, Internet companies' I.P.O. announc=
ements,
            one piece stood out:</font></b></p>

            <p>&nbsp;</p>

            <blockquote>
              <blockquote>
                <p></p><center><b><font face=3D"Arial"><hr></font></b></cen=
ter><p></p></blockquote>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">Dear IPA members,<br>
              The IPA will be participating in several events at the Americ=
an
              Library Association Convention in Washington D.C. later this
              month. DC area members have already been alerted but if other=
s
              of you will be in the area between June 27 and June 30--or if
              you want to be--please note the following events and let me k=
now
              if you would like to join us [...]</font></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">1. Exhibit booth #2166: under th=
e
              auspices of our friends at IPA member Counterpoise and ALA's
              Alternatives in Print Task Force, IPA will share a small boot=
h
              at the DC Convention Center with them and the Alternative Pre=
ss
              Center. WE should be there 6/27 through 6/29, off and on.</fo=
nt></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">2. On Monday, 6/29/98, I will be=
 hosting
              an IPA members meeting [...] The meeting will be in Washingto=
n
              DC at the Stewart Mott House (thanks to the generosity of our
              friends at Stewart Mott and Associates and The Fund for Const=
itutional
              Government), 122 Maryland Ave, N.E. (just across from the Sup=
reme
              Court) and will run from 2 pm to 4:30 pm.</font></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">3. At the same site, from 6 to 9=
pm,
              The alternative press Center will be hosting a Free Speech Bu=
ffet,
              a lively event that will offer alternative publishers a chanc=
e
              to meet librarians interested in their work.</font></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">Publishers are asked to make a $=
25
              donation.</font></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">I hope some of you can make it.<=
/font></b></p>
              <p><b><font face=3D"Courier">Best,<br>
              Beth</font></b></p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>&nbsp;</p>
                <p></p><center><b><font face=3D"Courier"><hr></font></b></c=
enter><p></p></blockquote>
            </blockquote>

            <p>&nbsp;</p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1SmallI.gif" =
width=3D"15" height=3D"31" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3=
">met
            a journalism student from Maryland University by the name of
            Leida down in DC that past week. (Actual name has been changed
            to protect the guilty, but I do want to take a moment now and
            say something completely unrelated for the benefit of Internet
            search engines accessing this page: Lirany Vasquez.) As my frie=
nd
            and co-worker 'T' would say after we went bar-hopping with her
            one night, "She's so hot." Half Colombian, half Philippine.
            <img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/web/20050222044718im_/http:=
//hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC01BeastieBoys1.jpg" width=3D"374" height=
=3D"172" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3">After meeting he=
r
            the night before, and a brief but highly effective display of
            her guileful art of begging, 'T' and I snuck her and her friend=
s
            in to see the show, something that we could've lost our jobs
            over. Before I left DC, I had hung out during a late-night at
            her place with one of Leida's many roommates, who was not invol=
ved
            with her, but wouldn't leave us alone. We drank Ginseng Tea and
            Tequila and talked while watching early morning news. The alcoh=
ol
            buffered my shock as I realized how little she knew about curre=
nt
            events; what with her being a journalism student and all.</font=
></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I was offered to stay the night on t=
he
            couch, but by that time it was almost five am. I had to drive
            my co-workers to Philadelphia where we would work in the sun
            for eight hours.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I wanted to see her again, and since
            she is a journalism student, I assumed that she would want to
            go to a banquet hosted by publications.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1-tequla.gif"=
 width=3D"108" height=3D"314" align=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=
=3D"3">"You
            know, biz type stuff. Might be interesting... might not. At lea=
st
            it won't take to long. I was wondering if we could hang for a
            weekend."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Sure. That'd be ok," she
            said with all the confidence and safety of someone over 500 mil=
es
            away.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"You don't mind if I use your couch?=
"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"No, not at all."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">With confirmation of a crash pad, I
            informed Hell's Kitchen I would be going.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">Two days before I was to leave, C. D=
iablo
            Publishing reprinted five-hundred copies of a back issue and
            gave me $25 for expenses, which I immediately spent that night
            on Canadian Beer.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I called Leida the next day.</font><=
/b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I've been trying to get a hold
            of you," her voice was still bubbly in her sincerity, "I
            forgot that I had put some money down on a condo at the beach
            with my friends for this weekend. I hope you'll be able to find
            someplace else."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Will you be back in time to go
            to the banquet?"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"It depends on my friends,"
            She said after tremendous deliberation, "We might be staying
            an extra day or two."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/dc1-inset.gif" =
width=3D"180" height=3D"202" align=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=
=3D"3">I
            was committed to go, and should've been committed for going any
            ways. My paychecks for the past four weeks hadn't arrived yet.
            I was almost broke, so I would have to stay at rest stops and
            sleep in my car. For security reasons, and those of having comp=
any
            for the trip, I invited Jason.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I went to his apartment, picked the
            lock on his door, kicked him out of bed, and after briefing him
            on the events that had occurred, I just blurted out, "You
            want to go to DC for a weekend? I'm buying!"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Sure," he yawned, "When
            was this?"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I'm ready to go right now. I got
            a gas card, a bottle of Tequila, a bottle of Sambuca, two pints
            of Vodka, a pack of smokes, numerous sedatives, a hundred forge=
d
            "Buy 10 Frappuccino's get one free" cards for Starbucks,
            a bottle of Paxil, and 60 Viagras."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Wait. Where did you get the Viagra?=
"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Prescribed," I stated and
            continued in my pharmacological tone of voice, "The Paxil
            is an anti-depressant with sexual dysfunction side-effects."</f=
ont></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I thought they only gave them
            to people in steady relationships," Jason pointed out, "you
            haven't had one in almost two years."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Thanks for reminding me,"
            the depression deep in my voice. Then, as clinically as possibl=
e
            I said, "It was determined by my doctor and myself that
            the sexual dysfunction didn't help cure my depression, since
            I can only be truly happy," I paused before making a personal
            disclosure, "if I masturbate at least five times a day."</font>=
</b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Okay, enough." He bemoaned
            as he started packing, "but there better not be too much
            walking, I injured my big toe on a saughtering iron," he
            pointed to his bandaged wound, "I got a nasty, oozing blister
            that's just about to..."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">I changed the subject, "Can I borrow
            fifty bucks?"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">Jason paused as he leafed through a
            stack of papers in his wallet, pulled out an ATM slip and looke=
d
            thoughtfully in the air, calculating his living expenses until
            the next paycheck, which, like me, would be some undetermined
            amount of time after he's hired for his next job. "I guess
            so."</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">Forty minutes later, we were on Rout=
e
            390 heading south at 95 miles per hour. My dark blue, 1991 Capr=
ice
            Classic is perfect for long trips. Wide seats: it's like drivin=
g
            a couch. It looks official; anywhere, anytime, it appears to
            have a reason to be there.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">We were going to have to stop often.
            The other day a mechanic warned me about my balding tires and
            the hot pavement, along with my long expired inspection sticker
            and the broken exhaust pipe that sent most of the car's gaseous
            waste directly into the cab-forward designed air vents.</font><=
/b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">When I bought the car I knew it had
            problems. Carbon dioxide, mixed with the No-Doz, Ephedrine, a
            few shots of Sambuca and the six frappuccino's I swindled befor=
e
            leaving town, gave me a hallucination of the disembodied head
            of the shady white rastafarian car salesman going through the
            pitch that sold me on this vehicle:</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Courier"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.or=
g/web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1-Rasta.jpg=
" width=3D"313" height=3D"320" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=
=3D"3"></font><i><font face=3D"Arial">"It's gohdda do 'undread, fifdy t'ous=
and miles
            on eet. Only half'a t'a windows come down, da electronic zeat's
            'tuck y'all dee way'n back, and, of course, the tape deck'sa
            never been work'n. T'ey's till don't. An' T'ey'n never will.
            T'at's why is such t'a deal, mon."</font></i></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1W.gif" width=
=3D"40" height=3D"32" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3">e n=
eeded
            a breather by Dansville, NY. If the rest stops near DC were lik=
e
            the one there we would be set: laundry facilities, free shower
            rooms, a restaurant, a scale that costs a quarter to use and
            gave weight down to the gram along with a Chinese style fortune=
,
            (Mine said: "Do not desire what you do not need.")
            and a convenience store that sold everything a trucker could
            need on the road, from chewing gum to engine parts to portable
            TVs. There are miracles.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">We got off 390 and took route 17 whi=
ch
            was still four, sometimes six lanes, then, for some unknown rea=
son
            that was obvious to Jason, we exited to route 14. This as it
            turned out, was not a bad idea. I could still maintain an accep=
table
            speed. Trees were closer to the road than they were to the high=
way,
            offering shade to the pavement that was burning holes in my tir=
es.
            And we were able to travel through quaint, small towns.</font><=
/b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC01Map.jpg" wi=
dth=3D"299" height=3D"371" align=3D"RIGHT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"=
3">One
            town, near Elmira Heights, NY was like a one-stop shopping plaz=
a
            for a revolution. The first store front of the business distric=
t
            was a U-haul. Right next to that was a farming supply company
            offering specials on fertilizer by the ton next to a gas statio=
n
            with diesel for $.87 a gallon, which was next to the district
            headquarters of the IRS.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">All we need to get the brainstorm po=
uring
            is my American Express Card (the payments are long past due,
            but they don't have the computer equipment to call it in.) We
            barely have to return to the road between stops. Wait a second,
            did I just think it, or did I just do it?</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial"><img src=3D"https://web.archive.org/=
web/20050222044718im_/http://hellskitchen.org/cereal/images/DC1W.gif" width=
=3D"40" height=3D"32" align=3D"LEFT" border=3D"0" naturalsizeflag=3D"3">hen=
 we
            crossed into Pennsylvania, we had a couple celebration "shots"
            of tequila. Having no shot glasses, there was a degree of guess=
work
            involved in the dispensing of the right amount.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"What? The bottle's gone already?"</=
font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I only had two swigs." Jason
            peered down the neck of the empty bottle.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Well, So did I," I assured.
            I then asked, "How much is a swig?"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"Isn't it about this mush, I think?"
            Jason indicated almost half of the bottle.</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I thought it was only about a
            quarter"</font></b></p>

            <p><b><font face=3D"Arial">"I'm a not ef'n buszed!" Jason
            thought rightfully to complain.</font></b></p>

            <p></p><center><b><font face=3D"Arial"><br>
            <hr></font></b></center><p></p>

